<title>ESTONIA: TRADE IN RAKVERE TO RESTART.</title>
<headline>TRADE IN RAKVERE TO RESTART.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tallinn stock exchange will restart trade in Rakvere meat factory shares from the bourse opening, bourse managing director Helo Meigas said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We found that investors have enough information,&quot; Meigas told Reuters.</p>
<p>The share was suspended yesterday so that investors would have time to digest news that the police are investigating alleged insider dealing in its shares.  </p>
<p>The investigation was linked to trading in Rakvere's shares on May 14/15, when it rose sharply ahead of an announcement that it was to buy a majority stake in a leading Latvian meat firm, Rigas Miesnieks.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
